kwin: let nested-backend virtual outputs exist, with or without OpenGL

Two fixes to `zkde_screencast_unstable_v1.stream_virtual_output` on a kwin
running nested under another compositor (pixelflux), where Selkies grows this
session's screens through that request and captures them from the host side,
never consuming the PipeWire stream.

1. `WaylandBackend::createVirtualOutput` creates the output and its host
   window but never adds it to `m_outputs` nor emits
   `outputAdded`/`outputsQueried` — only the startup `createOutputs()` path
   does that bookkeeping. The workspace therefore never realizes the output,
   the screencast manager's `workspace()->findOutput()` returns null ("Could
   not find output"), and the orphan's host window is a surface kwin never
   composites into. `removeVirtualOutput` already performs the symmetric
   removal. The DRM and virtual backends do the equivalent bookkeeping, which
   is why the desktop portal's virtual monitors work on real sessions.

2. `streamVirtualOutput` refuses outright under non-OpenGL compositing, but
   the check protects only the PipeWire capture (`ScreenCastStream` records
   through GL); the output itself composites fine under QPainter. Reordered so
   the output is created and bound to the stream's lifetime first, with the
   check still gating the capture: a GL-less session gets a live screen and an
   honestly failed stream, and the GL-dependent recording machinery still
   never runs where it cannot.

Applies to kwin 6.6.x (verified against v6.6.6).

--- a/src/plugins/screencast/screencastmanager.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/screencast/screencastmanager.cpp
@@ -77,16 +77,17 @@ void ScreencastManager::streamVirtualOutput(ScreencastStreamV1Interface *stream,
                                             double scale,
                                             ScreencastV1Interface::CursorMode mode)
 {
+    auto output = kwinApp()->outputBackend()->createVirtualOutput(name, description, size, scale);
+    connect(stream, &ScreencastStreamV1Interface::finished, output, [output] {
+        kwinApp()->outputBackend()->removeVirtualOutput(output);
+    });
+
     if (!isSupportedCompositingType()) {
         stream->sendFailed(i18n("Unsupported compositing type"));
         return;
     }

-    auto output = kwinApp()->outputBackend()->createVirtualOutput(name, description, size, scale);
     streamOutput(stream, workspace()->findOutput(output), mode);
-    connect(stream, &ScreencastStreamV1Interface::finished, output, [output] {
-        kwinApp()->outputBackend()->removeVirtualOutput(output);
-    });
 }

 void ScreencastManager::streamWaylandOutput(ScreencastStreamV1Interface *waylandStream,
--- a/src/backends/wayland/wayland_backend.cpp
+++ b/src/backends/wayland/wayland_backend.cpp
@@ -600,7 +600,11 @@ QList<BackendOutput *> WaylandBackend::outputs() const

 BackendOutput *WaylandBackend::createVirtualOutput(const QString &name, const QString &description, const QSize &size, double scale)
 {
-    return createOutput(name, size * scale, scale, false);
+    WaylandOutput *waylandOutput = createOutput(name, size * scale, scale, false);
+    m_outputs << waylandOutput;
+    Q_EMIT outputAdded(waylandOutput);
+    Q_EMIT outputsQueried();
+    return waylandOutput;
 }

 void WaylandBackend::removeVirtualOutput(BackendOutput *output)
